1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,050
Excuse me.

2
00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:01,650
Yes?

3
00:00:01,650 --> 00:00:05,130
I wonder if you could spare a few minutes to do a survey on

4
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:06,920
transport.It won't take long.

5
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:07,958
No,

6
00:00:07,958 --> 00:00:08,670
that's fine.

7
00:00:08,670 --> 00:00:09,312
Lovely.

8
00:00:09,312 --> 00:00:12,558
The survey is on behalf of the local council.

9
00:00:12,558 --> 00:00:18,000
They'd like to know about what transport you use and any suggestions for improvement.

10
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,920
Can I start by asking you how you travelled to town today?

11
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:22,292
Sure.

12
00:00:22,292 --> 00:00:24,150
I came on the bus.

13
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:24,532
Great.

14
00:00:24,532 --> 00:00:27,970
Now can I get a few details about yourself?

15
00:00:27,970 --> 00:00:28,560
OK.

16
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:29,940
What's your name?

17
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:31,360
It's Luisa ....

18
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:32,160
Yes.

19
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:32,660
Hardie.

20
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:34,200
Can you spell that, please?

21
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,890
Yes, it's H-A-R-D-l-E.

22
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:38,444
Great.

23
00:00:38,444 --> 00:00:38,998
Thanks.

24
00:00:38,998 --> 00:00:42,320
And can I have your address?

25
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:45,240
It's 19, White Stone Road.

26
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:45,964
Oh, right.

27
00:00:45,964 --> 00:00:47,412
I know that area.

28
00:00:47,412 --> 00:00:48,860
It's Bradfield, isn't it?

29
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:50,110
That's right.

30
00:00:50,110 --> 00:00:52,320
Is the postcode GT7?

31
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:55,480
It's actually G-T-8 2-L-C.

32
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:55,787
Great.

33
00:00:55,787 --> 00:00:58,242
And could I ask what your job is?

34
00:00:58,242 --> 00:00:59,470
Are you a student?

35
00:00:59,470 --> 00:01:01,723
I've actually just finished my training.

36
00:01:01,723 --> 00:01:02,850
I'm a hairdresser.

37
00:01:02,850 --> 00:01:03,539
Oh, right.

38
00:01:03,539 --> 00:01:05,953
And one more question in this section.

39
00:01:05,953 --> 00:01:09,400
What is the reason for you coming into town today?

40
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:11,426
Actually it's not for shopping today,

41
00:01:11,426 --> 00:01:13,452
which would be my normal reason,

42
00:01:13,452 --> 00:01:15,140
but to see the dentist.

43
00:01:15,140 --> 00:01:16,605
Right.

44
00:01:16,605 --> 00:01:18,070
Thanks.

45
00:01:18,070 --> 00:01:23,976
Now in this last section I'd like you to give us some ideas about the facilities

46
00:01:23,976 --> 00:01:29,144
and arrangements in the city for getting to and from work, er, any suggestions

47
00:01:29,144 --> 00:01:30,620
you have for improvements.

48
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:35,655
Well, something I've thought about for some time is that when I do walk

49
00:01:35,655 --> 00:01:40,330
and I'm doing a later shift, I think the lighting should be better.

50
00:01:40,330 --> 00:01:41,630
Yes, good point.

51
00:01:41,630 --> 00:01:45,294
And of course, I think it's a real shame they've been cutting down on

52
00:01:45,294 --> 00:01:46,341
the number of footpaths.

53
00:01:46,341 --> 00:01:47,911
They should have more of those.

54
00:01:47,911 --> 00:01:49,220
Then people would walk more.

55
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:50,170
Yes, right.

56
00:01:50,170 --> 00:01:52,362
And, I don't think there are enough trains.

57
00:01:52,362 --> 00:01:55,650
That's why I don't use them - you have to wait so long.

58
00:01:55,650 --> 00:01:55,958
Thanks.

59
00:01:55,958 --> 00:01:59,041
And finally I'd like to ask your opinion on cycling.

60
00:01:59,041 --> 00:02:03,357
As you may know, there's a drive in the city to get more people

61
00:02:03,357 --> 00:02:04,590
to cycle to work.

62
00:02:04,590 --> 00:02:05,150
Right.

63
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:08,241
But we realize that there are things which the council,

64
00:02:08,241 --> 00:02:12,260
but also employers, might do to help encourage workers to cycle to work.

65
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:12,584
Yep.

66
00:02:12,584 --> 00:02:17,128
Well, I have thought about it and where I work there are no safe

67
00:02:17,128 --> 00:02:18,750
places to leave your bikes.

68
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:19,770
OK.

69
00:02:19,770 --> 00:02:24,855
And also, I'd have to cycle uphill and on a hot day l'd arrive at work pretty sweaty

70
00:02:24,855 --> 00:02:27,680
so I think I'd need a shower somewhere at work.

71
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:28,290
Right.

72
00:02:28,290 --> 00:02:32,833
And I suppose the last thing is that I wouldn't be all that confident

73
00:02:32,833 --> 00:02:34,780
about cycling on such busy roads.

74
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:38,526
I think I'd like to see you offering training for that, you know, I'd

75
00:02:38,526 --> 00:02:41,470
feel a lot better about starting if that was the case.

76
00:02:41,470 --> 00:02:41,811
Well,

77
00:02:41,811 --> 00:02:42,834
that's very helpful.

78
00:02:42,834 --> 00:02:45,220
Thank you very much for your time.

79
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:46,800
No problem, bye!
